# Paths the PR reviewer does not read (SERV-87).
#
# One extended regex per line, matched against the repository-relative path of
# every changed file. `#` comments and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Per-repo on purpose even though the workflow is shared (SERV-92): which
# artifacts are generated is a fact about this repository. The shared workflow
# reads this from the BASE ref of the PR under review, so widening it in a PR
# does not exempt that PR — and this path is in `sensitive_paths`, so the PR
# proposing the edit gets the deeper pass.
#
# What belongs here is regenerated artifacts, not merely large files. The test
# is: if this file is wrong, is the fix to edit it? For a generated file the
# answer is no — you re-run the generator — so a review comment on its diff has
# nowhere to land. A large hand-written file is exactly what the reviewer should
# be spending its budget on.

# release-please owns both of these and rewrites them wholesale. A release PR
# touching only these is already skipped a rule earlier, by the release-PR test
# that derives its expected set from `release-please-config.json`; this covers
# the case where one rides along with code. `CHANGELOG.md` is also `.md`, so the
# docs-only rule would catch it alone; the manifest would not.
^CHANGELOG\.md$
^\.release-please-manifest\.json$

# NOT excluded, deliberately, and each for a reason:
#
#   go.sum        — a dependency tree, but also the checksum database. A line
#                   moving here without a matching go.mod change is the shape of
#                   a supply-chain problem, and that is worth a read.
#   migrations/   — hand-written SQL, applied automatically at boot by the
#                   in-process migrator. In `sensitive_paths`.
#   docs/architecture.md — 676 lines of hand-written design record. The
#                   docs-only rule already skips a PR that touches nothing else;
#                   excluding it here would also drop it from a code PR, where
#                   a design doc contradicting the diff is the finding.
#   deploy/Dockerfile, deploy/construct-server.compose.yml, Makefile — hand-
#                   written build and deploy definitions, and the place the
#                   version string has to agree with `internal/version` and
#                   `publish.yml` character for character (PRSR-32).
